    "sourceWrites": false,
    "height": "Record row span comes from physical column structure. Vertical groups sum their parts; horizontal groups take their maximum and InCell remains a single row. Caption bands stay in the rendered header but do not increase the data row budget. Font conversion rounds each stacked data band before summing.",
    "footer": "The existing keyed logical column projection also supplies the footer. Vertical fields keep their own cells, horizontal groups share tracks, and InCell keeps one composite cell. With limited height the compound footer keeps its bands and the header can be clipped. Empty horizontal groups keep their XML identity and produce no footer cell.",
    "scope": "Height metrics are Linux-specific. The logical compound footer projection is shared. Windows geometry and the full profile are unaccepted."
  },
